@bio:

Martin Rohrmeier is Associate Professor of Musicology at
the École Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne (EPFL),
where he directs the Digital and Cognitive Musicology Lab
(DCML). He studied philosophy, musicology, and mathematics
in Bonn and completed his MPhil and PhD at the University
of Cambridge under the supervision of Ian Cross. His
research interests bridge formal music theory, cognitive
science, and computational methods, with a focus on
mathematical and generative models of musical structure,
large-scale empirical music analysis, as well as
computational creativity. He has been co-directing a major
initiative dedicated to open, expert-annotated symbolic
music corpora.


@@END: BIO